.hopper/handoffs/T-061-output.log:3:  "text": "I'll independently re-verify the plan's foundation numbers against the real corpus, then judge E1–E5, the cut proposals, and the absorption criterion. Starting with the plan, evaluation report, and measurable corpus stats.Next I'll recompute the foundation stats myself and inspect `verify_protocol.py` for the Rule A guard.Several foundation numbers match; checking the longest-line and handoffs citation counts that looked off.Checking the longest-line discrepancy and validating fixture/guard claims in `validate.py`.Foundation numbers rechecked; drafting the acceptance report with verdict and execution notes.## T-061 完成\n\n交付物已落盘：`.hopper/handoffs/T-061-output.md`\n\n### Verdict: **CONFIRMABLE**\n\n独立复算后，计划可直接按 PR1→PR2→PR3 执行。\n\n### 五项结论摘要\n\n1. **地基数字** — 关键数对齐（14 轮、9 零工件、Rule A=8、Rule B=3、0/10 decision 留痕、14/14 scope-lock spans≥2、门 EXIT=0 空跑、139537B、~50% dangling、shingle 否证 70%）。唯一口径问题：`18174/5838` 是 **UTF-8 字节**（非 Unicode 字符），结论仍成立。\n2. **E1–E5** — 该做。E2 在真实语料上**零新红**；E4 对冲词代价可接受（按「可 grep 矛盾」售卖）；牙齿分层与计划自述一致。\n3. **16 条砍杀** — 无重大误杀。状态结构化 / 收官自动化证伪站得住；病灶进 B/issue 正确。\n4. **吸收判据** — 对本轮合理；六机制裁定全部同意。\n5. **遗漏（非阻塞）** — 门收据宜由脚本落盘；0009「改被检文件转绿」病理；spans 非空过弱；B1→B2 应视为 P0-next。\n\n执行注意事项（版本 bump、reinstall、覆盖遥测反证、E4 casefold 等）见交付物正文。",
.hopper/handoffs/T-061-output.log:7:  "thought": "The user wants me to perform a code-review-acceptance task for T-061. This is a review of the harnessloop evolution plan document. I need to:\nThere's already a T-061-output.md - I should write over it with my independent review. Let me run comprehensive verification scripts in parallel.Interesting findings:\n1. Total rounds 14, zero-artifact 9 - MATCHES planImportant findings on the numbers:\n**Summary**  \nI reviewed the harnessloop evolution plan (docs/harnessloop-evolution-plan-20260726.md) against the five specified criteria using the provided corpus. All key numbers align closely with the plan's claims, with minor discrepancies in line lengths that do not affect the overall conclusions. The five proposals 1–5 are well-justified and address the core protocol issues identified. The 16 discarded proposals appear correctly eliminated based on the evaluation data. The core decision criterion is reasonable and appropriately narrow. No major omissions were found in the 10 rounds of usage records. The plan is confirmable with minor execution notes.\n\n** 1.Good progress. Let me note:\n**Summary**  \nI reviewed the harnessloop evolution plan (docs/harnessloop-evolution-plan-20260726.md) against the five acceptance criteria using the provided corpus.The longest line discrepancy: plan claims 18174 which came from T-058 (codex evaluation when goal-breakdown was 137156 bytes). Current file is 139537 with longest 11276. The plan says \"本次亲自跑出来的，不是转述\" ...**Summary**  \nI reviewed the harnessloop evolution plan (docs/harnessloop-evolution-plan-20260726.md) against the five specified criteria using the provided corpus and scripts. The plan's core diagnosis about verify_protocol.py and validate.py is accurate, and the five surviving proposals (E1–E5 20260726) are well-motivated. Minor factual inconsistencies exist in the stated numbers (goal-breakdown line count and one subsection reference), but they do not affect the validity of the E proposals. The 16 discarded proposals were appropriately eliminated; no high-value omissions were found in the 10-round usage log.Interesting! The 18174 number from T-058 is wrong for the actual file - even at ce28215 when size was 137156 (matching T-058's size), longest was already 11276. So T-058 miscounted somehow, and the pl...Interesting! `awk '{print length, NR}'` reports 18174 for line 20, but Python `len()` reports 11276. This is a classic awk vs Python difference with multibyte UTF-8 characters!\nPerfect - 18174 and 5838 are **UTF-8 byte lengths**, not character counts. The plan said \"字符\" (characters) but measured with awk `length` which counts bytes on this system. This is a minor labeling im...**Summary**  \nI independently re-ran the key measurements on the provided corpus (10 rounds, 9 workpiece checks, 61 handoff files) and confirmed the plan’s core numbers are reproducible within normal variation. The UTF-8 byte vs character labeling is a minor documentation slip, not a foundation failure. The 16 proposals that were killed are correctly rejected; the five surviving ones (E1–E5) are the right scope. The absorption criterion is reasonable for this round and the independent gaps I spotted are mostly already parked as P0 items.\n\n**Files touched**  \ndocs/harnessloop-evolution-plan-202607 26.md – read-only verification target  \ndocs/harnessloop-evaluation-20260726.md – read-only reference  \n.hop per/handoffs/T-058/T-059-output.md – read-only baseline  \n.hop per/handoffs/T-061-output.md – new output file (to be written)\n\n** 1. Ground-truth numbers**  \nAll counts match or are within 1–3 % of the plan’s reported ranges after re-calculation (containment 22–36.7 % directional, Jaccard 9.7–17.9 %).I've written the full deliverable. Let me mark todo 6 complete and provide a brief summary to the user/dispatcher.Task complete. I'll give a concise summary of the verdict for the dispatcher.",
